        "message": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "reasoning",
              "text": "R3 定稿: the gap faces downward (bottom). The ring is open at the bottom, like \"∩\" shape. Gap faces down.\n\nCurrent version R43: gap faces right (like \"C\").\n\nSo answer: the saved final version (定稿 R3) has the gap facing down/bottom; the current draft (R43) rotated so gap faces right. Should note the difference clearly since the user is looking at the current version simultaneously.\n\nLet me be careful: R3 image shows an arc open at bottom — two tips pointing down at bottom-left and bottom-right, with the opening between them at the bottom. Yes, gap at bottom/down.\n\nAnswer concisely."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "我核对过了，结论和当前稿不一样：\n\n- **定稿（R3「潮汐图标 · 定稿」）：缺口朝下**。它是一个环，上半部完整，左右两端向下收尾，开口落在**正下方**（大致是 6 点钟方向），两个端点分别在下方的偏左和偏右位置。\n- 当前稿（R43）：同样的环体，但缺口在**正右方**（3 点钟方向），整体看起来像字母 “C”，相当于定稿的基础图形顺时针旋转了 90°。\n\n所以：**保存的定稿缺口朝下，当前这版朝右**。如果当前稿是要跟定稿对齐，这里就需要把图形逆时针转 90°，让开口回到正下方；如果这次是有意改成朝右，那就和定稿不一致了，建议确认哪一版是基准。"
            }
          ],
          "source": {
